# Decompose the GraphBackend god-class into focused mixins

## Context
`interfaces/GraphBackend.py` had grown to 1170 LOC — the single largest class in
the graph DB layer and well over the 800-LOC architecture budget. It mixed the
core read contract (abstract methods + capability flags + connection/schema/sync
hooks) with a huge pile of concrete default-SQL implementations (stats,
entity/preview lookup, traversal/reasoning, companion probing). Split the
default implementations into four cohesive mixins so the root class carries only
the contract, with zero behavioural change (every subclass inherits the exact
same methods by composition).

## Changes
1. `src/back/core/graphdb/interfaces/ReadStatsMixin.py` — new. `ReadStatsMixin`:
   `get_inferred_triple_count`, `_distinct_count_expr`, `get_aggregate_stats`,
   `get_type_distribution`, `query_triples_for_analysis`,
   `_filter_analysis_triples_in_python`, `get_predicate_distribution`.
2. `src/back/core/graphdb/interfaces/EntityQueryMixin.py` — new.
   `EntityQueryMixin`: `find_subjects_by_type`, `resolve_subject_by_id`,
   `get_entity_metadata`, `get_triples_for_subjects`,
   `get_triples_page_for_subjects`, `get_predicates_for_type`,
   `paginated_triples`, `paginated_count`, `find_seed_subjects`,
   `find_preview_seeds`, `find_subjects_by_patterns`.
3. `src/back/core/graphdb/interfaces/TraversalMixin.py` — new. `TraversalMixin`:
   `bfs_traversal`, `transitive_closure`, `symmetric_expand`, `shortest_path`,
   `delete_cohort_triples`, `expand_entity_neighbors`.
4. `src/back/core/graphdb/interfaces/SearchCacheMixin.py` — new.
   `SearchCacheMixin`: `search_cache_mode`, `_companion_tables_exist`,
   `set_search_cache_mode`, `_raise_if_force_on_missing`, `_props_table_for_read`,
   `adjacency_table_ids`, `rebuild_adjacency`, `adjacency_ready`,
   `entity_search_table_id`, `entity_search_asserted_table_id`, `props_table_id`,
   `entity_search_ready`.
5. `src/back/core/graphdb/interfaces/GraphBackend.py` — reduced to the read
   contract; now `class GraphBackend(ReadStatsMixin, EntityQueryMixin,
   TraversalMixin, SearchCacheMixin, ABC)`. Keeps the abstract methods, SQL
   helpers (`_sql_escape`/`_sql_relation`/`sql_table_reference`/`sql_flavor`),
   capability flags, schema/sync hooks, and `get_query_translator`. Class drops
   out of the oversized-classes baseline entirely.
6. The mixins are implementation detail (not exported by `interfaces/__init__.py`,
   `Mixin` suffix, "implementation detail" docstrings). Files are named after
   their class to satisfy the one-class-per-file architecture rule
   (`test_class_per_file`), which overrides the underscore-private file naming.
7. `tests/units/graphdb/test_graphdb_adjacency_contract.py` — patch target for
   `props_page_sql` moved to the `EntityQueryMixin` module.
8. `tests/units/architecture/baseline.json` — ratchet removed the stale
   `GraphBackend` oversized entry (shrink-only).

## Modified files
- `src/back/core/graphdb/interfaces/GraphBackend.py`
- `src/back/core/graphdb/interfaces/ReadStatsMixin.py` (new)
- `src/back/core/graphdb/interfaces/EntityQueryMixin.py` (new)
- `src/back/core/graphdb/interfaces/TraversalMixin.py` (new)
- `src/back/core/graphdb/interfaces/SearchCacheMixin.py` (new)
- `tests/units/graphdb/test_graphdb_adjacency_contract.py`
- `tests/units/architecture/baseline.json`

## Tests
`uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` → **9865 passed, 326 skipped**
(explicit `EXIT=0`). Architecture class-per-file + size-budget + ratchet green.
